  ### Step 1: Inspect the Disk Image & Find the User Directory
  First, find where the main file system lives:

    # Check the partition layout
    mmls disk.flag.img
  What you see:
  • Partition 1: Boot sector (Offset 2048)
  • Partition 2: Linux Swap (Offset 206848)
  • Partition 3: Linux ext4 (Offset 731136) — The main root filesystem

  List the files in user yone's home directory using SleuthKit (fls) or Autopsy:

    fls -o 731136 disk.flag.img 24

  You find 5 interesting directories:

  • gallery/ → Four bitmap images: 1.bmp, 2.bmp, 3.bmp, 7.bmp.
  • notes/ → Three text notes: 1.txt, 2.txt, 3.txt.
  • irclogs/ → Date folders containing IRC chat logs.
  • .lynx/ → Lynx web browser history.
  • Maildir/ → Email messages.
